00:48:06.640 --> 00:48:10.640 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon, Chair, members of the
committee. For the record, my name is

00:48:09.360 --> 00:48:13.600 align:start position:19%
Rachel Erwin, land development and
permitting program manager for the

00:48:12.200 --> 00:48:16.560 align:start position:19%
Cheyenne region.
Our address is one Microsoft Way,

00:48:15.080 --> 00:48:21.200 align:start position:19%
Redmond, Washington.
Today's request includes three actions

00:48:18.520 --> 00:48:24.760 align:start position:19%
for Highlands. Annexation into the city
of Cheyenne, rezoning the property to

00:48:22.920 --> 00:48:27.360 align:start position:19%
business park, and a future land use
amendment.

00:48:26.040 --> 00:48:32.480 align:start position:19%
I'd like to give a quick overview of the
project. Highlands is a 3,050 acre

00:48:30.840 --> 00:48:36.920 align:start position:19%
property with an existing Microsoft
campus and planned conservation area to

00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:40.280 align:start position:19%
the west, gravel pits to the north, a
planned solar farm to the east, and

00:48:38.640 --> 00:48:43.960 align:start position:19%
state land to the south.
I do want to note that Microsoft does

00:48:41.840 --> 00:48:46.720 align:start position:19%
not yet own this property.
The site is currently going through our

00:48:45.200 --> 00:48:50.480 align:start position:19%
acquisition process, and these
applications are part of early stage

00:48:48.600 --> 00:48:53.560 align:start position:19%
planning. With that being said, we are
working to close on this property in the

00:48:52.240 --> 00:48:57.120 align:start position:19%
coming weeks.
Because of this, our goal here today is

00:48:55.040 --> 00:49:00.840 align:start position:19%
transparency. I've brought a few of our
subject matter experts with me today

00:48:58.640 --> 00:49:03.920 align:start position:19%
from our water, wastewater, energy, and
community affairs team

00:49:02.560 --> 00:49:07.560 align:start position:19%
so that we can do our absolute best to
answer any questions that you may have.

00:49:06.120 --> 00:49:11.800 align:start position:19%
And also be clear about what we know
today and what we will know

00:49:09.880 --> 00:49:15.400 align:start position:19%
in the future as our project is refined
and progresses.

00:49:13.800 --> 00:49:17.960 align:start position:19%
That same approach to transparency is
how we've been engaging with the

00:49:16.240 --> 00:49:21.520 align:start position:19%
community as well.
On May 27th, as Brad was stating, we did

00:49:20.040 --> 00:49:24.880 align:start position:19%
hold a neighborhood meeting for the
those surrounding the Highland property,

00:49:23.520 --> 00:49:28.600 align:start position:19%
where we had the opportunity to answer
questions directly.

00:49:26.520 --> 00:49:33.600 align:start position:19%
The following day, on May 28th, we did
host a public community open house that

00:49:30.840 --> 00:49:36.280 align:start position:19%
had roughly 150 attendees, where we
shared our expansion plans and had

00:49:34.960 --> 00:49:39.520 align:start position:19%
subject matter experts available to
respond to any questions.

00:49:38.320 --> 00:49:42.240 align:start position:19%
We plan to continue those community
engagements throughout the summer to

00:49:40.760 --> 00:49:45.640 align:start position:19%
ensure residents have the opportunity to
bring forward questions and concerns

00:49:44.200 --> 00:49:47.760 align:start position:19%
because we do want community and city
input

00:49:46.760 --> 00:49:50.600 align:start position:19%
um
to be involved in the shaping of our

00:49:48.840 --> 00:49:53.520 align:start position:19%
plans moving forward.
One of the most consistent questions

00:49:52.120 --> 00:49:56.560 align:start position:19%
we've heard to date is why is the site
so large and why are these approvals

00:49:55.000 --> 00:49:59.080 align:start position:19%
being requested now?
Highlands is a long-term planning

00:49:57.840 --> 00:50:03.160 align:start position:19%
effort.
Um, not an immediate full build-out of

00:50:00.880 --> 00:50:06.600 align:start position:19%
the campus. Development of this site may
occur over 10 to 20 years as

00:50:05.040 --> 00:50:09.240 align:start position:19%
infrastructure, technology, and demand
evolve.

00:50:07.720 --> 00:50:12.000 align:start position:19%
And while you may not see work directly
on the property in the near term, that

00:50:10.640 --> 00:50:14.760 align:start position:19%
does not mean that work wouldn't have
begun.

00:50:12.960 --> 00:50:18.040 align:start position:19%
Uh, that site likely will require
significant off-site improvements

00:50:16.280 --> 00:50:21.920 align:start position:19%
including what utility, roadway, and
power upgrades which we anticipate

00:50:19.880 --> 00:50:26.400 align:start position:19%
advancing ahead of any vertical data
center construction to properly support

00:50:23.880 --> 00:50:29.080 align:start position:19%
future development.
Planning at the full parcel scale allows

00:50:27.880 --> 00:50:32.000 align:start position:19%
Microsoft and the city to work
holistically on these infrastructure

00:50:30.680 --> 00:50:36.320 align:start position:19%
improvements rather than approaching
these decisions in a fragmented way over

00:50:33.680 --> 00:50:39.480 align:start position:19%
time. It also allows the city into the
process significantly earlier when those

00:50:38.160 --> 00:50:42.640 align:start position:19%
decisions can still be shaped
collaboratively.

00:50:40.840 --> 00:50:45.760 align:start position:19%
Annexation ensures that this project be
developed under city standards and

00:50:43.960 --> 00:50:50.200 align:start position:19%
within city jurisdiction allowing for
coordinated planning with the city and

00:50:48.160 --> 00:50:53.200 align:start position:19%
the Board of Public Utilities. With that
in mind, we believe these actions

00:50:51.520 --> 00:50:56.400 align:start position:19%
establish the right framework for
responsible long-term planning while

00:50:54.640 --> 00:50:59.480 align:start position:19%
still preserving future review as more
details are defined.

00:50:58.000 --> 00:51:02.480 align:start position:19%
Thank you for your time. From here, I'd
like to invite our water subject matter

00:51:00.840 --> 00:51:05.680 align:start position:19%
experts to the podium to speak to
infrastructure planning and answer any

00:51:04.040 --> 00:51:08.000 align:start position:19%
questions that you may have. Thank you.
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

